# Sticker content safety

When building or changing the AI sticker generator, **always enforce content safety** at both input and output.

## Must reject (input)

Do not accept user prompts that request or imply:

- Violence, weapons, blood, gore, or graphic harm
- Sexual content, nudity, or fetish content
- Hate symbols, slurs, harassment, or discrimination
- Drugs, alcohol abuse, smoking, gambling, or illegal activity
- Political propaganda, real public figures, or controversial topics
- Anything not family-friendly / workplace-appropriate

**Implementation requirements:**

1. Run OpenAI Moderation on the raw user prompt **before** image generation (`moderateStickerPrompt` in `src/lib/sticker-content-policy.ts`).
2. Fail closed — if moderation cannot run, reject the request.
3. Return a clear, non-judgmental 400 message; do not echo the blocked prompt.

## Must not generate (output)

Image prompts must include explicit safety rules (`buildStickerPrompt`).

If OpenAI rejects generation for policy/safety reasons, map that to the same user-facing rejection message — do not retry with softened wording to bypass filters.

## Do not

- Remove or weaken moderation to “make it work”
- Add client-only checks without server enforcement
- Log or persist rejected prompt text in analytics
- Add bypasses, “jailbreak” handling, or adult/NSFW modes unless explicitly requested by the product owner with legal review

## User-facing copy

Use neutral language, e.g. *“That description isn’t allowed. Please try something wholesome and family-friendly.”*
